---
description: Android Kotlin and Compose rules
globs:
  - "android/**/*.kt"
  - "android/**/*.kts"
  - "android/**/*.xml"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3 and Hilt.
- Follow unidirectional data flow: UI event -> ViewModel -> use case/repository -> immutable UI state.
- Composables must not call network or database APIs directly.
- Keep navigation arguments minimal; load business data through ViewModel/use cases.
- Every screen must define loading, content, empty and recoverable error states.
- Preserve unfinished assessment/training state across process recreation where feasible.
- Audio recording uses an explicit state machine.
- Request microphone permission only when the user starts a voice action.
- Put user-visible strings in Android resources.
- Accessibility: meaningful content descriptions, minimum touch targets and readable contrast.
- Add ViewModel tests and Compose UI tests for critical flows.
